  "meta": {
    "space": "embeddings_ability.npy",
    "projection": "classical MDS + SMACOF, canonically oriented",
    "clustering": "average-linkage agglomerative on cosine distance, 2 levels",
    "cards": 80,
    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "city-1, city-4 and city-1's single child are one-neighbourhood cities: hood-0 is byte-identical to its parent (8/8, 8/8). I left those hood ids unnamed rather than invent a synonym for the city above them; the renderer's fallback is the honest answer there.",
      "city-3's split reads arbitrary to me. Thirteen lands sit in hood-0 and three in hood-1 (Bojuka Bog, Cabal Coffers, a Swamp), and I cannot state a job those three share that the other thirteen lack: Coffers is the deck's biggest mana engine, the Swamp is a Swamp, and the Bog is graveyard hate. Both hoods left to the fallback.",
      "city-5-hood-1 is the two-card outlier and it is real, not noise. Neither Grave Pact nor Plumb the Forbidden drains, which is what every other card in that city does. Plumb the Forbidden is the deck's most unusual card by the map's own measure: card_roles.json assigns it no role at all (deck-facts lists it and Supernatural Stamina as the only two role-less cards), so it has nothing to be near. It belongs in the 99 as wrath insurance; it just has no neighbours.",
      "city-2 is where the mass is (21 of 80 mapped entries) and the mass is doing one thing: manufacturing repeat deaths. Ten cards reuse a body, seven make bodies in batches, four buy a body back from the graveyard. Two of the three declared engine pieces live here, in different neighbourhoods (Gravecrawler in hood-0, Nest of Scarabs in hood-1); the third, the commander, is in city-0.",
      "city-2-hood-0 has four members that are neither bodies nor recursion: Lightning Greaves, Jet Medallion, Necropotence, Skullclamp. Greaves and the Medallion are the least at home under any name I could give that neighbourhood; they are commander support (haste on the turn he lands, and a discount), not a second use of a creature. I named for the seven-card majority and am flagging the four.",
      "Sol Ring is the odd member of city-0-hood-0: it is there as a mana rock beside Ashnod's Altar and Phyrexian Altar, which are outlets that also make mana. The clustering read the mana, not the outlet.",
      "city-4 carries a verified_count of 1 (Fume Spitter) against city-5's 7 and city-0's 4. The interaction city is almost absent from the verified kill lines, which matches the deck's shape: the answers and the kill are separate machines, and only the counter-based half of the removal feeds the kill (Nest of Scarabs sits one city over).",
      "city-3 is the only city with zero verified cards. That is expected of a land city and I read nothing into it."
    ]
  },
